  "notes": "Recorded at Atlantic Recording Studios, New York, N.Y.\nAdditional recordings at A & R Studios, New York, N.Y., Atlantic Recording Studios, New York, N.Y. & Kaye/Smith Studios, Seattle, Washington.\n\nManufactured and Distributed under license from WEA Records Pty. Ltd.\n℗ © 1973 Atlantic Recording Corporation\n\nOn labels:\n℗ 1973\nManufactured in Australia by a registered user of the trademark.\n\nPublishers (On Labels only):\nTracks A1, A5, B1, B2: Albert\nTrack A2: Warner Bros.\nTracks A3, B4: Control\nTrack A4: GEMA-Control\nTrack B3: Belinda\nTrack B5: Jewel\n\nPublishers (On Sleeve only):\nTrack A1: Carmichael Music-Mercer Music\nTrack A2: Warner Bros.\nTrack A3: Ordena Music-Bridgeport Music\nTrack A4: Weill-Brecht-Harms\nTrack A5: Dwarf Music\nTrack B1: Leo Feist; Warner Bros.\nTrack B2: Shapiro, Bernstein\nTrack B3: Mother Bertha\nTrack B4: Prestige\nTrack B5: Jalynn-Chevis-BRC\n\nOn spine:\nDistributed by WEA Records Pty. Limited\n\nThe catalog# SD-7270 appears on the labels, whilst the catalog# SD 7270 appears on the rear sleeve.\nThis release varies from the other Australian Bette Midler, self-titled release in the database in that the cat# containing a dash (ie. '-' between the SD and the 7270) is what appears here on the labels, whereas the other release doesn't feature a 'dashed' cat# at all (being SD7270 on the labels).\nAs well as this, there are some minor text layout variations on the labels, such as the Rights Society for track B4 (Surabaya Johnny) being here for GEMA-Control, whilst the other release it is for GEMA/MCPS. However, in all other respects, including the Runouts, the two releases are otherwise near-identical.\n\nThis version appears to be a Reissue.\n\nB3. Thomas McKinney credited in error as songwriter for \"Uptown\", correct songwriters are Barry Mann & Cynthia Weil.\n\n",
